From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Return to Flashforge firmware on Kiln OS

Settings > System gets "Return to Flashforge firmware" under Boot into
recovery: after a confirmation it calls Moonraker's
machine.kiln_os.return_stock (Kiln's kiln_os component), which restarts
the printer into the recovery OS and has it offer putting Flashforge's
own firmware back. Nothing is written until that is tapped on the
recovery screen; the confirmation says so. Like Boot into recovery, the
request goes over the screen's own connection to Moonraker (127.0.0.1),
the row is greyed while a print is active and shows only on Kiln OS
builds (HELIX_KILN_AD5X, the same kiln_boot_recovery_available subject).

The answer {"state": "rebooting", "result": "rebooting"} is read from
"state", or "result" when there is no state. A refusal is shown without
Kiln's "[reason] " in front, and without the update agent's older
"Update agent: ", "refused: " and "failed: " prefixes (Boot into
recovery shows its refusals the same way now). Boot into recovery and
the new row share the request and confirmation code. Strings in en and
ru.

Tests: the method name, the rebooting answers (state and result, each
alone), a refusal with and without the reason as data, an unexpected or
empty answer; the row's callback, its visibility and greying.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
